WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.790
As early as August 2010, early warning
systems forecast a likely emergency in

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.950
Somalia.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.390
On 20 July 2011, the UN declared famine.

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:18.850
An estimated 258,000 people died
between October 2010 and April 2012.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.950
The warning came first.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.370
So why didn't it prevent disaster?

7
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.810
Were the warnings wrong?

8
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.390
Was there no food anywhere in Somalia?

9
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.770
In this mission, you'll
learn what counts as famine:

10
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.550
three thresholds that must
all be met in one area.

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.930
Then you'll test Amartya Sen's
ideas about famine against Somalia,

12
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.070
and ask whether lessons
were learned by 2022.

13
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:48.430
Your mission: explain why a warning in
August 2010 did not prevent famine in 2011.
